/-!
# Natural-module calculations for SL₂(4)

This interface exposes the actual binary natural module, compatible Frobenius
actions, canonical-field transport, fixed-space calculations, and transitivity
on nonzero vectors and hyperplanes. Its 35 binary planes comprise five
Sylow-central F₄-lines and three noncentral SL₂-orbits of length ten, classified
by their nonzero binary-basis determinants.

The full binary normalizer is the actual semilinear group ΓL₂(4), inducing S₃
on those three orbits. The subgroup generated by SL₂ and coordinate Frobenius
is identified with S₅ by its action on the five F₄-lines. In this S₅ there are
ten field-type planes and a single type-3 orbit of length twenty. In the full
normalizer all thirty noncentral planes are field type, and there is no
type-3 orbit. Field type uses the original field involutions and their actual
fixed subspaces.

Source: Aschbacher--Smith, *The Classification of Quasithin Groups*, §6.2,
printed pp.680--681, PDF pp.697--698. These are the natural-module calculations
in 6.2.2 and 6.2.5; the ambient-group arguments remain with the chapter owner.
-/
